:rel-1152921504606847695 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-719;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-437;
  :comment " The text describes a system where agents visit farms to calculate and secure provisions, specifically bread grain, with the remaining amount collected for distribution, implying a centralized system of resource allocation and collection. This system is set in World War I Germany given the context of wartime food supply in the 19th and early 20th century.";
  :id "3a91e59c-74a0-46ad-a8d1-5ff9fcf15c9d";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

:rel-1155173304420532943 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-719;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-624;
  :comment " The summary details visits to farms to calculate and secure provisions, check pre-prepared, weighed, and documented items, and ensure farmers show all rooms and confirm they had no other bread grain in stock before signing a protocol. This level of inspection and control is a direct example of official scrutiny of rural food supplies as it would have been practiced in 20th-century Germany during periods of scarcity, such as the World Wars.";
  :id "7045be6a-0297-4b6e-943d-e750293c46de";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

