:rel-1157425104234218699 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-1227;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-265;
  :comment " Maslov is quoted criticizing \"the Workers' Council for hindering the war effort and causing internal disunity\" and proposing \"the Workers' Council form commissions for organizing economic life.\" Lenin and his comrades are also mentioned as heading to Petersburg to advocate for peace, the republic, and socialism, implying a significant role for such councils.";
  :id "46fa1239-c83e-4ee4-9bac-042573a51275";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

:rel-1155173304420533451 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-1227;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-269;
  :comment " The text mentions \"The Petersburg Congress of the Cadet Party experienced unrest regarding the threatened provisional government,\" and \"Chairman Prince Dolgorukov stated the necessity of changing the party program for upcoming elections, as Russia's rapid democratization made the Cadet Party's goals seem backward.\" This directly addresses the challenges to and perceived diminishing legitimacy of the Provisional Government.";
  :id "adf76a9e-daab-4b4b-a8f6-8d69571e55c7";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

:rel-1159676904047903947 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-1227;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-271;
  :comment " Kokoshkin \"advo cated transitioning from demanding a constitutional monarchy to a parliamentary republic, asserting that the republic already existed in fact.\" Lenin and his comrades are also mentioned as advocating for \"peace, the republic, and socialism.\" These highlight the ideological shifts and debates surrounding the revolutionary government.";
  :id "96d81f2b-d990-47fa-9748-7f771ba283b5";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

