  :comment "The \"population of the United States, insofar as it could directly enrich itself from the flood of gold that, thanks to the massacre of peoples, found its way across the great water, today accepts the momentous step of its chief official with chauvinistic sentiments, as a great patriotic act. But it is only a small fraction of Americans who sit at the rich table of war profits\" suggests that a large part of the population, especially the working class, is disillusioned. The text also mentions Woodrow Wilson and the war." .

