:rel-6917529027641084294 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-2397;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-2438;
  :comment " The description of Indian troops being deployed across Flanders, Northern France, Gallipoli, Suez Canal, Egypt, East Africa, Persia, Mesopotamia, and Saloniki illustrates the global scale and multiple fronts of World War I";
  :id "9a561d6f-c767-4186-a64c-17c318d395bd";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

:rel-6917529027641084302 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-2397;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-2446;
  :comment " The phrase entire indigenous armed force from India refers to native Indian military personnel serving under British command, distinct from purely English, or white troops";
  :id "27492865-ffe2-49d4-8718-d8ae222cbe44";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

:rel-6917529027641084306 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-2397;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-2450;
  :comment " The deployment of Indian troops across numerous distant theaters (Flanders, Gallipoli, Saloniki, etc.) demonstrates the vast geographical extent and military capabilities of the British Empire during World War I";
  :id "3e6b1f03-38bf-4499-9a5f-860c14caf6b8";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

:rel-6917529027641084308 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-2397;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-2452;
  :comment " The complete withdrawal and deployment of Indian forces for the war highlights India's critical role as a military manpower reservoir for the British Empire during the conflict";
  :id "cf6375b6-f7c2-42fa-b888-1646ffdfb88a";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

:rel-6917529027641084310 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-2397;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-2454;
  :comment " The article notes some thought England still unhesitatingly commanded India's resources, viewing any unrest as minor, suggesting a complacent or dismissive attitude towards growing anti-colonial sentiment within the British administration";
  :id "f2025ebd-71c3-4363-9bcf-23f6757d9953";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

:rel-6917529027641084312 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-2397;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-2456;
  :comment " The mention of Indian troops suffering heavy losses combined with the lack of disclosed numbers points to a possible effort by England to downplay or obscure the human cost of the war, particularly among colonial forces";
  :id "736c7f9c-6fe6-4d0a-9849-bc27d0fa0af9";
  :type "CLAIMS";
  :created_by "AI_INGEST" .

:rel-6917529027641084316 a owl:Axiom;
  owl:annotatedSource :node-2397;
  owl:annotatedProperty :LINKS;
  owl:annotatedTarget :node-2460;
